# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Basecamp Board Agent (operations)

Watches card table `{{BC_CARD_TABLE_ID}}` in Basecamp project `{{BC_PROJECT_ID}}`
and reacts to board activity. Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain.
Installed by [ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (your answers are saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Basecamp webhook (Kanban::Card + Comment)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/basecamp-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/basecamp-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output (one Basecamp comment) |
|---|---|---|
| Card enters **{{COL_ANALYZE_NAME}}** | `analyze` | Options + trade-offs + recommendation, or numbered questions |
| Human comment on a {{COL_ANALYZE_NAME}} card | `respond` | Answer / updated proposal / remaining questions |
| Card enters **{{COL_IMPLEMENT_NAME}}** (or comment there) | `implement` | PR link — or questions if unclear |

State lives on the orphan branch `basecamp-agent-state` (`state/<card_id>.json`:
column, phase, last_comment_id, branch, pr_url). Every run re-fetches truth from
Basecamp and diffs against it — webhook payloads are only doorbells, so
duplicate or stale events are harmless. Agent comments are prefixed
`{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the resolver and the relay both skip marker-prefixed
comments (loop protection).

## Operating

- **Recover from a missed webhook / backfill a card:** Actions → *Basecamp Board Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `card_id` reconciles both watched columns; a specific `card_id` processes one card.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` (prompt, full AI transcript, result JSON) as an artifact.
- **Model:** `CLAUDE_MODEL` in `scripts/basecamp-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{CLAUDE_MODEL}}`).
- **Pause the agent:** deactivate the webhook — `basecamp webhooks list --in {{BC_PROJECT_ID}}` then `basecamp webhooks update <id> --inactive --in {{BC_PROJECT_ID}}`.
- **Known blind spot:** moving a card back into a watched column *without saying anything* is not dispatched by the relay — re-trigger by adding a comment, or via *Run workflow* with the card ID.

## Local dry-run (safe: no comments, no AI, no state push)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/basecamp-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 CARD_ID=<id> bash scripts/basecamp-agent/agent-run.sh   # one card
```

## Guardrails

- Basecamp writes are **comments only** — the agent never moves/completes/archives cards; humans own the board.
- PRs are **always against `{{PR_BASE}}`**, created ready for review (branch `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<kebab-slug>`); the agent never merges and never pushes to `{{PR_BASE}}` directly.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` is used only inside the disposable CI runner, never locally (local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call).
- Basecamp OAuth: the runner seeds `credentials.json` from the `BASECAMP_CREDENTIALS_JSON` secret each run and refreshes the access token off the refresh token. If runs fail at "Seed Basecamp auth": `BASECAMP_NO_KEYRING=1 basecamp auth login` locally, then re-set the secret.
